simulation. Each was a caller-free second implementation of a live job and three disagreed numerically with it; the debt they recorded is paid by deletion, not by a fix. 2026-08-22: pruned 4 data_io entries that the text oracle recorded from prose, not code (entities_3d nib.load, optional_imports h5py.File, infer.py h5py.File + nib.load) — infer.py's docstring asserts the pipeline layer never calls them and the regex read that sentence as the violation. The scanner is now AST-based, so the list can only shrink. 2026-08-22: training_loop grew 1 -> 6 entries (8 occurrences) WITHOUT any new code -- TARGET_METHODS is now derived from base.py's own per-step call graph instead of being a four-name literal, three of whose names were defined zero times anywhere under strategies/. The real hook _compute_losses_impl (144 definers) had never been audited. Entries now carry a count: identity alone forgives a whole method, which is the NN20 hole where growth inside a baselined entry goes unseen. 2026-08-22 (#1398): layer_direction gained the three OUTER source layers (infrastructure, application, pipelines) as this test was elected sole owner of import direction and the matching emit blocks were deleted from scripts/ci/check_layering.sh. The extension surfaced exactly 2 violations, both function-local at col 8 in hpo_use_case.py -- the shape the deleted greps could never see. infrastructure -> application is a rule NEITHER checker had; it measured 0 violations, so it lands as a pure ratchet with no baselined debt. 2026-08-23 (D12#5): training_loop grew 6 -> 10 entries, again WITHOUT any new code -- the detector gained an implicit-sync visitor for 'if' tests that boolean a tensor ('.any()'/'.all()' and torch.isnan/isinf/isfinite), which no '.item()' spelling makes visible. Exactly 4 sites, recorded one per 'if' rather than one per matching call (the 'isnan().any() or isinf().any()' expression matches four times and is one sync point; counting calls would have inflated the report to 7). Bare-name any()/all() are deliberately NOT matched -- as a bare name they are the Python builtins over a generator, and 3 sites in the audited methods depend on that. Correcting the count above: _compute_losses_impl is defined in 134 files (145 definitions), not '144 definers'. 2026-08-24 (D01#16): renamed the scripts_imports key to nonpackage_imports and widened its scanner from the single hardcoded name 'scripts' to NONPACKAGE_ROOTS (scripts, scratch, runners, tools, tests) -- every repo-root tree absent from pyproject's packages=[\"src/spectramr\"]. It had recorded 0 violations since it was written while 2 real ones sat at cli/app.py:474,487 (col 8, function-local), which break spectramr list-features on every wheel install. Recorded here as one entry (both sites are the same file+import); the relocation of tools/generate_feature_matrix.py and tools/feature_introspection.py into the package is filed as #1492. The scanner skips relative ImportFrom nodes: ast drops the leading dots, so 'from .tools import x' arrives as the bare name 'tools' and the first-segment match condemned a legal in-package import of src/spectramr/tools/.",
